// src/v4/extdeps/languages/rust.dag
//
// Scope: Rust target language spec — primitives, syntax, codegen rules.
// Anchor: https://doc.rust-lang.org/reference/ (Rust Reference) — the
//         versioned upstream specification (L-2 fidelity authority).
//         The Reference is the spec the carriers below are pinned to;
//         when the Reference changes (a new edition adds / renames a
//         primitive; the stable IEEE-754 width set grows; a new
//         visibility scope), the change is a visible C1 edit to the
//         relevant declaration below, never a silent extension.
// Unifies: (per THESIS:188) language spec = transport spec = interpreter
//         runtime. ONE substrate carrier for all three roles. Different
//         lenses read different facts from the same data (emission
//         reads syntax; transport reads serialization; interpreter
//         reads execution semantics). A worker needing transport or
//         runtime extends this file, not a new "transport spec" file.
//
// STRUCTURAL FINDING (this slice's deliverable, manager directive
//   msg_4f7e1280 — the operator-critical-path T-4 directive, item 3;
//   reinforced msg_8b477982).
//   Rust's TYPE-SYSTEM SURFACE — scalar primitive vocabulary, reference
//   kinds, visibility scopes — fits the substrate's existing
//   classifier shape (closed Disj + Conj records) without modification.
//   No 7th connective, no 6th behavior is surfaced by this slice. The
//   slice declares the Rust type VOCABULARY as Node-shaped declaration-
//   class data; it deliberately STOPS at the carrier-shaped seams where
//   D1 (parse/emit operations — ratified Outcome<T> = Produced { value:
//   T } | Rejected { diagnostic: Diagnostic }, NOT YET LANDED in
//   std/diagnostic.dag) and D2 (per-language primitive inhabitance
//   instance-values + fn-value-expression form — operator-pending
//   SEMANTIC decision, msg_640d429c; §0 ratifies v2-syntax legality
//   only, NOT the inhabitance shape per msg_8b477982) plug in.
//
//   The seams are NAMED in "Owned ELSEWHERE" below with their owners
//   and dissolution triggers. Authoring those seams here would have
//   improvised past D1/D2 — exactly the keen-wren-419 (T-4.6) /
//   loyal-koi-702 (T-4 languages) STOP-and-escalate precedent
//   established 2026-05-16. Deferral-with-named-trigger, never
//   improvisation.
//
// Owns (this slice — REVISED from scaffold; scaffold's "Rust primitives
//   with algebra inhabitance" + "emission rules" + "cost realization"
//   lines are PRESERVED AS GOALS in the Owns→ELSEWHERE table below;
//   the slice-vs-bundled split is explicit, not silent — same revision
//   discipline as ptx.dag #3170):
//
//   - Rust scalar primitive vocabulary as closed structural carriers:
//     RustIntKind (signed / unsigned), RustIntWidth (Bits8/16/32/64/
//     128 + Pointer for isize/usize per std/machine.dag PointerWidth),
//     RustFloatWidth (Bits32/64 — the stable Rust IEEE-754 width set;
//     f16/f128 are unstable per the pinned Reference), RustScalarKind
//     (the Int/Float/Bool/Char/Str/Never primitive-types partition
//     per Reference §3.3-§3.6; `()` is a TupleType per §3.10 and is
//     out-of-scope for this slice — see SCOPE NEGATIVE Tuple types)
//   - Rust scalar typed-shape sum: RustScalar (kind × width as a Disj
//     with named-field variant payloads — illegal kind×width pairs are
//     STRUCTURALLY UNREPRESENTABLE: no "Bool with width=Bits32",
//     because Bool/Char/Str/Never variants carry no width payload)
//   - Rust reference vocabulary: RustReferenceKind (Shared / Exclusive
//     — Rust's `&T` vs `&mut T`), and the Conj carrier RustReference
//     attaching it to an opaque lifetime Symbol (K-1) AND the
//     referent Node (the Reference's TypeNoBounds slot) — three
//     coordinates total per `&'lifetime mut? TypeNoBounds`, so
//     `&'a i32` and `&'a str` are distinct facts (P1/P2 fidelity)
//   - Rust visibility scope: RustVisibility (Private / Pub / PubIn
//     { path: List<Symbol> }) — the three-way visibility partition
//     reflecting the Reference's fundamental form
//     (§visibility-and-privacy), with `pub(crate)` / `pub(self)` /
//     `pub(super)` folding into PubIn's path-list per the Reference's
//     stated equivalences. Path-restricted visibility CARRIES its
//     SimplePath structurally; `pub(in crate::outer_mod)` is
//     representable.
//   - Rust per-target cost-realization carrier shape: RustCost (per-
//     instruction + per-allocation components — the per-target
//     projection U1 reads; the carrier SHAPE only, no instance-values
//     pre-T-3 / pre-D2)
//
// Owned ELSEWHERE (deliberately NOT in this slice — named owners +
//   dissolution triggers per directive item 3 "DEFER explicitly, with
//   named owner + dissolution trigger"):
//
//   - Rust scalar inhabitance instance-values: `data rust_i32_ring:
//     OrderedRing<I32> = OrderedRing { ... }` and the parallel rows
//     for the 11 other integer types, IEEE-754 widths, Bool, Char,
//     Str, Never. RIDES the operator D2 form-decision (msg_640d429c —
//     STOP-2/STOP-3 escalated by loyal-koi-702; brief §B's per-
//     language inhabitance form conflicts with INVARIANTS P1:42's
//     `Compose<Int, MachineWidth<Word*>>` worked example, AND the
//     fn-value-expression form for spec-primitive operations
//     (3a/3b/3c — name-reference Atom vs relaxed instance vs new
//     substrate carrier) is unspecified). §0 ratifies v2-SYNTAX
//     LEGALITY ONLY; per-target inhabitance shape is a SEPARATE
//     operator-pending SEMANTIC decision (manager reinforcement
//     msg_8b477982). AND rides std/integer.dag / std/float.dag /
//     std/logic.dag / std/text.dag (T-3 wave A3) carrier landing for
//     P2 single-authority: pre-D2 / pre-T-3 inhabitance would
//     foreclose the eventual canonical authority.
//     STOP-TRIGGER (named, binding): authoring even a "placeholder"
//     `data rust_i32_ring: OrderedRing<...> = ...` row here pre-D2
//     is the FORBIDDEN deferral (the v3 cross-layer-drift failure
//     mode this file's restraint exists to prevent). The PR #3171
//     improvisation-held draft is the precedent for what NOT to do
//     (manager held it to draft for exactly this reason). Stub-to-
//     keep-moving is forbidden; defer-with-named-trigger is the
//     legitimate form.
//     SEAM (where it plugs in): the closed RustScalar Disj declared
//     below is the SURFACE through which each Rust scalar's
//     inhabitance parameterizes — when D2 ratifies the instance-value
//     form AND T-3 wave A3 lands, the inhabitance rows land in this
//     file with the typed scalar variants below as their carriers.
//
//   - Bidirectional Rust LanguageModel substrate (grammar productions
//     as declarative B2-OMNI data, C5-fidelity disposition tags per
