//     operator D1 value-or-Diagnostic carrier — `Outcome<T> =
//     Produced { value: T } | Rejected { diagnostic: Diagnostic }`,
//     RATIFIED 2026-05-16 (manager reinforcement msg_8b477982,
//     ratified shape), NOT YET LANDED in std/diagnostic.dag. Parse /
//     emit operations cannot type their failure mode without it.
//     When the carrier lands AND the bundled LanguageModel shape
//     lands, this file's classifiers slot into the Rust
//     `LanguageModel` instance without revision; their I/O contract
//     is the immutable header above.
//     STOP-TRIGGER (named, binding): the temptation to STUB an
//     `emit_rust : Node -> Outcome<RustSource>` op here while D1 is
//     unlanded is the FORBIDDEN deferral (the v3 failure mode the
//     value-or-Diagnostic-STOP precedent foreclosed) — STOP and
//     surface, never stub. Stub-to-keep-moving is the exact shape
//     that broke v3; the named "Owned ELSEWHERE" note is the
//     legitimate deferral form (ptx #3170 precedent).
//     SEAM: the Rust grammar production data attaches as Node trees
//     in this file (B2-OMNI: grammar is data, not code); the carriers
//     declared here are the type-system structure the grammar
